  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Recovers from a Blend reserve reindex.\\n\\n`config.reserve_index` is fixed at init and the rate path traps with\\n`InvalidBlendReserve` whenever Blend has since moved the underlying to a\\ndifferent reserve slot. That fail-closed trap is correct (pricing the\\nwrong reserve would be worse), but on its own it is unrecoverable: every\\nrate read, and therefore every deposit/redeem/split/recombine, stays\\nbricked for the life of the market. This admin entrypoint re-syncs the\\nstored index to wherever the pool now keeps this wrapper's underlying.\\n\\nIt does NOT trust a caller-supplied index. It re-derives the index the\\nsame way `initialize_blend` does: it finds the underlying's position in\\nthe pool's reserve list and cross-checks that against the pool's own\\n`get_reserve(underlying).config.index`, and requires the reserve decimals\\nto still match. The new index is accepted only if the asset actually\\nsitting there is `config.underlying`. So the strongest thing an admin can\\ndo here is re-point the wrapper at the same underlying und",
      "name": "migrate_reserve_index",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "admin",
          "type_": "address"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "result": {
            "ok_type": "u32",
            "error_type": "error"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Withdraws the entire Blend position into idle custody and closes the\\nmarket permanently.\\n\\nThis exists because `config.pool` is fixed at init with no rotation. If\\nBlend pauses the reserve, deprecates it, or the wrapper's position\\nbecomes unreadable, then `exchange_rate` traps \\xe2\\x80\\x94 and with it deposit,\\nredeem, split, recombine, redeem_at_maturity and every AMM swap, since\\nthey all read it. Without this, that state is unrecoverable and user\\nfunds are stranded.\\n\\nAfterwards the rate is derived from idle custody exactly the way it was\\nderived from the Blend position (`assets * WAD / supply`), so it needs no\\nfrozen snapshot and no new failure mode, and `redeem` pays out pro-rata\\nfrom the recovered balance. Deposits are closed forever.\\n\\nIrreversible on purpose: allowing a return to Blend would make this a\\nrate-manipulation lever rather than a safety valve.",
      "name": "emergency_withdraw_all",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "result": {
            "ok_type": "i128",
            "error_type": "error"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
